From f51a00d5608a49d6606fd8efa52f717b441c9719 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kimolas <4828831+kimolas@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:58:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat: open plugin catalog books in the reader (download.open)

A JSON plugin catalog can set `download.open: true`. Confirm on a book row
then opens it in the reader: a copy already at the download destination
opens as is (no request; layout cache and reading position kept), otherwise
the book downloads as usual and then opens. Opening records the book in
state.json and reboots straight into it, the clean-heap reboot every Wi-Fi
screen does on exit. After a fresh download it first sends the queued
plugin events while Wi-Fi is still up, under a Loading popup; below the TLS
heap floor they wait for the next Wi-Fi join. If the book cannot be
recorded, a fresh download shows the download-complete screen and a copy
already on the card shows an error.

Bundle rows and files the reader does not open keep the Fetch label and the
download-complete screen; the rows that open read Open. Older firmware
ignores the key. Advertised as the capability catalog.open_after_download.

Also adds a `sendtox3` build env (version 2.0.0-sx3+<hash>).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
