+- **Open in reader** (`download.open`): Confirm on a book row opens it in
+  the reader. If the file the row would download to is already on the card,
+  it opens unchanged: no request, no `book.downloaded`, and its layout cache
+  and reading position are kept; any plugin events still queued wait for the
+  next Wi-Fi join. Otherwise the book downloads as usual (cache reset,
+  sidecar, Library marker, `book.downloaded`), then opens: a Loading popup
+  shows while the queued plugin events, the new `book.downloaded` among them,
+  are sent over the still-connected Wi-Fi (unless the heap is too low for
+  TLS; they then wait for the next join). Opening ends the catalog session:
+  the device reboots straight into the book (the clean-heap reboot every
+  Wi-Fi screen does on exit). An `.epub` at the destination that is not a
+  ZIP is downloaded again. Bundle rows and files the reader does not open
+  (anything but `.epub`, `.txt`, `.md`, `.xtc`) keep the Fetch label and the
+  download-complete screen; the Confirm label reads Open only on rows that
+  open.
+
+  The destination path is the book's identity: whatever file is already there
+  opens instead of the row's own download. Two rows share a file when their
+  names match after sanitizing. The rendered name is cut to 100 bytes, stem
+  first (a long title drops a trailing `{id}`); `/ \ : * ? " < > |` become
+  `_`, control characters are dropped, and leading and trailing spaces and
+  dots are trimmed; and the FAT card ignores case. A catalog whose titles may
+  collide should therefore put the id first, `"{id} {title}.epub"`, or use
+  `"{id}.epub"`; a row whose content changes needs a new id.
 - **After download**: the book's layout cache is invalidated and the optional
   sidecar is written. Use the `{dest}.meta.json` convention so the fields ride
   KOSync progress uploads and event handlers (see `plugin-events.md`).
